status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMURA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMOTAKA, KANTA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUJI, KEI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A golf club head (11) having an ellipsoid of inertia (12) using a gravity center (G) as its center, wherein, when the ellipsoid of inertia (12) is virtually cut off on a plane which passes through the gravity center of the golf club head (11) and is positioned in parallel with a face surface (11f), the major axis of a plane ellipse (13) appearing on the cut-off surface and a crossed line (15) of the cut-off surface with the ground (16) forms an angle  theta , the major axis extends from the ground (16) upward as it nears a toe portion (11t), the angle  theta  is set at 0.5 DEG  or more and 9.5 DEG  or less, and an aspect ratio (a/b) specified by the ratio of the length (a) of the major axis (13d) of the plane ellipse (13) to the length (b) of a minor axis (13e) is 1 or more and 4 or less.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une tête (11) de club de golf présentant une ellipsoïde d'inertie (12) utilisant un centre de gravité (G) en son centre. Lorsque l'on illustre l'ellipsoïde d'inertie (12) en section sur un plan traversant le centre de gravité de la tête (11) du club de golf et parallèle à une surface (11f), le grand axe d'une ellipse plane (13) apparaissant sur la surface en coupe et une droite (15) se coupent et forment un angle  theta  avec le sol (16). Le grand axe monte depuis le sol (16) à mesure qu'il se rapproche de la partie pointe (11t), l'angle  theta  est compris entre 0,5  DEG  et 9,5 DEG  et un rapport de forme (a/b), à savoir le rapport entre la longueur (a) du grand axe (13d) de l'ellipse plane (13) et la longueur (b) d'un petit axe (13e), est compris entre 1 et 4.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>